# Clone's "You may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the battlefield" is a replacement effect of its own
# (CR 614.1c, 707.2), and which replacement effects apply to a permanent entering is judged on "the permanent as it would
# exist on the battlefield, taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the
# permanent" (CR 614.12). With Humility out, Clone as it would exist there is a creature with no abilities, so it can't
# copy: Bot1 is not asked (the refusal "! Bot1.Accept" holds across Clone's resolution, while the Overseer is there to be
# copied), and Clone enters as itself, a Shapeshifter that Humility makes 1/1 - it does not die as its printed 0/0, and it
# is no Inspiring Overseer, so no enters trigger of one could happen either: Bot1 stays at 21.
# The control: Inspiring Overseer, cast on turn 1 before Humility, did gain Bot1 1 life and draw a card.

